Map key-order canonicalisation — TRIGGER on the unwrap error-bypass identity.

`lowerRangeAggregation` projects three mutually exclusive stream identities.
map_key_order_count_over_time.txtar covers the default one; this covers the
third, which a numeric unwrap post-filter selects: the identity becomes
`if(mapContains(attrs, '__error__'), <bypass>, <base>)`, and its base arm
inherits the raw store's physical key order just as the default identity
does. The canonicalisation wraps OUTSIDE the `if`, so one sort canonicalises
both arms.

Same shape as the default-identity trigger: one logical stream
{dc="eu", job="api"} delivered twice under two physical key orders, so
`count(...)` reports 2 without the fix and 1 with it.

-- query.logql --
count(sum_over_time({job="api"} | logfmt | unwrap latency | status > 100 [5m]))
-- seed --
CREATE TABLE otel_logs (
    Timestamp DateTime64(9),
    Body String,
    SeverityText LowCardinality(String) DEFAULT '',
    ResourceAttributes Map(String, String),
    LogAttributes Map(String, String)
) ENGINE = Memory;
INSERT INTO otel_logs (Timestamp, Body, SeverityText, ResourceAttributes) VALUES
    (toDateTime64('2025-12-31 23:59:00', 9), 'latency=5 status=200', 'INFO', map('dc', 'eu', 'job', 'api')),
    (toDateTime64('2026-01-01 00:00:00', 9), 'latency=7 status=200', 'INFO', map('job', 'api', 'dc', 'eu'));
-- expected_rows --
[
  ["", {}, "2026-01-01T00:00:01Z", 1]
]
